#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kppp; for callback"
msgstr "Konfiguriranje &kppp; za povratni poziv"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter is based on material provided by Martin H&auml;fner, "
"<email>mh@ap-dec717c.physik.uni-karlsruhe.de</email>"
msgstr ""
"Ovo poglavlje je zasnovano na materijalu koji je dao Martin H&auml;fner, "
"<email>mh@ap-dec717c.physik.uni-karlsruhe.de</email>"

#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:8
#, no-c-format
msgid "&UNIX; or &Linux; callback server"
msgstr "&UNIX; ili &Linux; povratnih poziva server"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section introduces &UNIX; (&Linux;) callback, and how &kppp; can be "
"configured to connect to a &UNIX; callback server, especially to a script "
"based &Linux; callback server"
msgstr ""
"Ova sekcija predstavlja &UNIX; (&Linux;) povratni poziv, i kako &kppp; može "
"biti konfigurisan za spajanje na &UNIX; povratnih poziva server, posebno na "
"skripti zasnovan &Linux; povratnih poziva server"

#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "An Introduction to callback"
msgstr "Predstavljanje povratnih poziva"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several reasons to consider using callback. Some of these are:"
msgstr ""
"Postoji nekoliko razloga za uzimanje u obzir korištenja povratnog poziva. "
"Neki od njih su:"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "To increase the security of your local network"
msgstr "Da bi se povećala sigurnost vaše lokalne mreže"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "To reduce expenses of external co-workers"
msgstr "Kako bi smanjili troškove vanjskih saradnika"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "To control telephone costs where calls are claimed as business expenses"
msgstr ""
"Za kontrolu telefonskih troškova gdje se pozivi vode kao troškovi poslovanja"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Think about someone calling the number of your dial in server, and then "
"cracking a password. Why bother to maintain a firewall for your internet "
"connection, if access to your network is that easy?."
msgstr ""
"Razmislite o nekome ko zove vaš broj na serveru, a zatim provaljuje lozinku. "
"Zašto zadržati vatrozid za internet konekcije ako je pristup na vašu mrežu "
"tako jednostavan?."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Callback software generally asks for your name, and then hangs up the line. "
"It then calls you back, usually at a number that is stored <emphasis>on the "
"server</emphasis> in a database. The client then picks up the phone line and "
"continues with the dial-in as if nothing had happened. The server now "
"requests your username and password, knowing that you are who you said you "
"were when you first dialled in, or at the least, you are where you said you "
"were. The connection is established normally, and the <application>pppd</"
"application> is started."
msgstr ""
"Softver za povratne pozive uglavnom pita za ime, a zatim prekine vezu. Onda "
"vas pozove nazad, obično na broj koji se čuva <emphasis>na serveru</"
"emphasis> u bazi podataka. Klijent zatim podigne telefonsku liniju i "
"nastavlja sa pozivima, kao da se ništa nije dogodilo. Server sada traži vaše "
"korisničko ime i lozinku, znajući da ste onaj koji ste rekli da ste bili "
"kada ste prvi put birali, ili u najmanju ruku, vi ste ondje gdje ste rekli "
"da ste bili. Veza se uspostavlja normalno, i <application>pppd</application> "
"je počela."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now the big question is, how to tell the client to pick up the phone, when "
"the server calls you back. Do you need a special program, such as "
"<application>mgetty</application>? The answer is, <emphasis>no</emphasis>, "
"you don't need a special client program. In general, any client can be used "
"for callback connections, you could even use an ordinary terminal program "
"such as <application>minicom</application> to connect."
msgstr ""
"Sada je veliko pitanje, kako da se kaže klijentu da podigne slušalicu, kad "
"vas server pozove nazad. Da li vam je potreban poseban program, kao što je "
"<application>mgetty</application>? Odgovor je, <emphasis>ne</emphasis>, ne "
"treba vam poseban program klijenta. U principu, bilo koji klijent može se "
"koristiti za povratni poziv veze, možete čak i koristiti običan terminal "
"program, kao što je <application>minicom</application> za povezivanje."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The only thing you have to do is tell your modem to <command>AutoAnswer</"
"command> the phone when a <computeroutput>RING</computeroutput> is detected "
"by the modem. This is done with the following modem command:"
msgstr ""
"Jedina stvar koju morate učiniti je reći modemu da <command>Automatsko "
"Odgovaranje</command> na telefon kada <computeroutput>ZVONI</computeroutput> "
"> otkrije modem. To se radi sa sljedećom modem komandom:"

#. Tag: screen
#: callback.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput><command>AT&amp;SO=1</command></userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput><command>AT&amp;SO=1</command></userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tells the modem to pick the phone up after one <computeroutput>RING</"
"computeroutput>."
msgstr ""
"Ovo govori modemu da odgovori na telefon nakon jednog <computeroutput>ZVONI</"
"computeroutput>."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Like a lot of other client programs, &kppp; checks to see if the connection "
"is closed by the server, and then stops the current session if a "
"<computeroutput>NO CARRIER</computeroutput> is detected. This, then, is the "
"real problem when setting up callback. <computeroutput>NO CARRIER</"
"computeroutput> will of course be detected the moment the callback server "
"hangs up the line. Some servers therefore use a special login program. So "
"how do you solve this problem? You tell your modem to show "
"<computeroutput>CARRIER UP</computeroutput> at all times (which causes no "
"problems if you tell the client to hang up the line.) You can do this with "
"the following modem command:"
msgstr ""
"Kao mnogo drugih klijent programa, &kppp; provjerava da li je veza zatvorena "
"od strane servera, a zatim zaustavlja trenutnu sesiju ako se otkrije "
"<computeroutput>NO CARRIER</computeroutput>. To je, dakle, pravi problem "
"prilikom postavljanja povratnog poziva.  <computeroutput>NO CARRIER</"
"computeroutput> će, naravno, biti otkriven u trenutku kad server povratnog "
"poziva prekine vezu. Zato neki serveri koristiti poseban program za "
"prijavljivanje. Dakle, kako riješiti ovaj problem? Recite vašem modemu da "
"pokaže<computeroutput>CARRIER UP</computeroutput>   u svakom trenutku (koja "
"ne izaziva nikakve probleme ako kažete klijentu da prekine na liniji.) "
"Možete napraviti ovo sa sljedećom modem naredbom:"

#. Tag: screen
#: callback.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput><command>AT&amp;C0</command></userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput><command>AT&amp;C0</command></userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to test this, you can first use an ordinary terminal program "
"such as <application>minicom</application>, and call your callback server, "
"to see what hapens."
msgstr ""
"Ako želite testirati ovo, možete koristiti obično prvo terminal program, kao "
"što su <application>minicom</application>, i pozovite vaš server za povratne "
"pozive, da vidite šta će se dogoditi."

#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kppp; setup"
msgstr "&kppp; uređenje"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So, now that you've seen the theory in action, how do you go about setting "
"up &kppp; to handle the connection?"
msgstr ""
"Dakle, sada kada ste vidjeli teoriju u akciji, kako obavljate postavljanje "
"&kppp; za rukovanje vezom?"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "The procedure is quite straightforward, as follows."
msgstr "Postupak je prilično jednostavan, kako slijedi."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First tell the modem to accept connections, and to not stop the negotiation "
"when the callback server hangs up the line for the first time. You can add "
"both these options in the <guilabel>Modem</guilabel> tab of the &kppp; "
"configuration, by adding to the option <guilabel>Dial String</guilabel> the "
"string <command>AT&amp;C0S0=1DT</command>"
msgstr ""
"Prvo recite modemu da prihvati veze, i da ne zaustavi pregovore kada server "
"povratnih poziva prekine vezu po prvi put. Možete dodati obje ove opcije u "
"<guilabel>Modem</guilabel> traku &kppp; konfiguriranje, dodavanjem opcije "
"<guilabel>Biraj Niz</guilabel> niz <command>AT&amp;C0S0=1DT</command>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are no other changes with configuration for &kppp;. If you meet "
"trouble with modem init and reset, check the <link linkend=\"callback-"
"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</link> section for more information."
msgstr ""
"Nema drugih promjena za konfiguracije od &kppp;. Ako naiđete na probleme s "
"modemom init i reset, provjerite <link linkend=\"callback-troubleshooting"
"\">Rješavanje problema</link> sekciju za više informacija."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Think about your server for a moment. Remember that &UNIX;, &Windows; and "
"Macintosh operating systems have differing opinions about how to end a line "
"in a text file, and therefore, in login procedures too. If you are "
"connecting to a &Windows; server, use <userinput>CR/LF</userinput>, if you "
"are connecting to a &UNIX; server, use <userinput>CR</userinput>, and if you "
"are connecting to a Macintosh server, use <userinput>LF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"Razmislite o vašem serveru na trenutak. Imajte na umu da &UNIX;, &Windows; i "
"Macintosh operativni sistemi imaju različita mišljenja o tome kako da se "
"okonča linija u tekstualnoj datoteci, a samim tim, i procedure "
"prijavljivanja. Ako se povezujete na &Windows; server, koristite "
"<userinput>CR/LF</userinput>, ako se povezujete na &UNIX; server, koristite "
"<userinput>CR</userinput>, a ako se povezujete na Macintosh server, "
"koristite <userinput>LF</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We are assuming for these instructions that you are calling a &Linux; "
"callback package which uses ordinary login (not <acronym>PAP</acronym> or "
"such)."
msgstr ""
"Pretpostavljamo za ove instrukcije kojima pozivate &Linux; paket povratnih "
"poziva koji koristi običnu prijavu (ne <application>PAP</application> ili "
"slično)."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the <guilabel>Authentication</guilabel> style in the <guilabel>Dial</"
"guilabel> tab of the account configuration to <guilabel>Script-based</"
"guilabel>"
msgstr ""
"Postavite <guilabel>Ovjera</guilabel> stil u <guilabel>Biraj</guilabel> "
"traku konfiguracije računa na <guilabel>Skripta bazirano</guilabel>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you have to build the login script. Editing of login scripts is one of "
"the very cool features of &kppp;. You can find it in the <guilabel>Login "
"Script</guilabel> tab of the <guilabel>Edit Account</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""
"Sada morate napraviti skriptu prijave. Uređivanje skripti prijave je jedna "
"od vrlo cool osobina &kppp;. Možete je naći u <guilabel>Prijava Skripte</"
"guilabel> trake <guilabel>Urediti Račun</guilabel>."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example, the user <systemitem>userxyz</systemitem> needs the "
"following script to be called. The callback server already knows the table "
"of names and their applicable phone numbers, so you select the phone number "
"to be used with an alias, for security purposes."
msgstr ""
"U ovom primjeru, korisnik <systemitem>korisnikxyz</systemitem> treba da "
"pozove sljedeću skriptu. Server za povratne pozive već zna tabelu imena i "
"njihovih važećih brojeve telefona, tako da birate telefonski broj koji će se "
"koristiti sa aliasom, iz sigurnosnih razloga."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each line, choose the criteria from the drop down list on the left of "
"the dialog, and type in the action in the text box on its right. Choose the "
"<guibutton>Add</guibutton> to add each line to the script. You can use "
"<guibutton>Insert</guibutton> to add a line into the middle of the script, "
"and <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> to delete a line if you made a mistake."
msgstr ""
"Za svaku liniju, odaberite kriterije iz padajuće liste na lijevoj strani "
"dijaloga, i ukucajte u okvir akciju na desno. Odaberite <guibutton>Dodaj</"
"guibutton> da dodate svaku liniju u skriptu. Možete koristiti "
"<guibutton>Ubaciti</guibutton> za dodavanje linije u sredinu skripte, i "
"<guibutton>Ukloni</guibutton> da bi obrisali liniju ako ste napravili grešku."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The entire script should look something like this (without the comments, "
"shown here starting with a #)"
msgstr ""
"Cijeli skripta treba izgledati ovako (bez komentara, ovdje prikazane počevši "
"od #)"

#. Tag: screen
#: callback.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expect       ogin:           <lineannotation># remember, we do ordinary "
"terminal login</lineannotation>\n"
"ID           \"\"              <lineannotation># kppp sends the id you "
"configured in\n"
"the main dialog</lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       for userxyz:    <lineannotation># a list of available numbers "
"is\n"
"shown, the user should choose one</lineannotation> \n"
"Send         userxyz-home    <lineannotation># the user wants to be called "
"back\n"
"on their home number</lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       ogin:           <lineannotation># The callback process is now\n"
"running, a new connection, and so a new login.</lineannotation>\n"
"ID\n"
"Expect       assword:        <lineannotation># Now send your password</"
"lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       &gt;            <lineannotation># Wait for the command prompt "
"(the\n"
"prompt may vary)</lineannotation>\n"
"Send         start_ppp       <lineannotation># this command starts the pppd</"
"lineannotation>"
msgstr ""
"Expect       ogin:           <lineannotation># remember, we do ordinary "
"terminal login</lineannotation>\n"
"ID           \"\"              <lineannotation># kppp sends the id you "
"configured in\n"
"the main dialog</lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       for userxyz:    <lineannotation># a list of available numbers "
"is\n"
"shown, the user should choose one</lineannotation> \n"
"Send         userxyz-home    <lineannotation># the user wants to be called "
"back\n"
"on their home number</lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       ogin:           <lineannotation># The callback process is now\n"
"running, a new connection, and so a new login.</lineannotation>\n"
"ID\n"
"Expect       assword:        <lineannotation># Now send your password</"
"lineannotation>\n"
"Expect       &gt;            <lineannotation># Wait for the command prompt "
"(the\n"
"prompt may vary)</lineannotation>\n"
"Send         start_ppp       <lineannotation># this command starts the pppd</"
"lineannotation>"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After waiting for the login request, the user sends his ID and waits for a "
"list of available phone numbers for that username. Then he tells the server "
"which of the numbers offered he would like to be called back on. &kppp; can "
"open a dialog for this, if your location changes often, &eg; you are a sales "
"representative and move from hotel to hotel. Now the server is expecting "
"login and password for authentication, but in the meantime, the server hangs "
"up and calls the user back. The authentication information is sent, and "
"&kppp; waits for a command prompt, and then starts a small script (here "
"called <filename>start_ppp</filename> which fires up <application>pppd</"
"application> on the server."
msgstr ""
"Nakon čekanja na zahtjev za podnošenje prijave, korisnik šalje svoj ID i "
"čeka listu dostupnih telefonskih brojeva za to ime. Onda govori serveru koji "
"od ponuđenih brojeva bi volio da ga zovu nazad. &kppp; može otvoriti dijalog "
"za ovo, ako se vaša lokacija mijenja često, &eg; Vi ste predstavnik prodaje "
"i idete od hotela do hotela. Sada server očekuju prijavu i lozinku za "
"ovjeru, ali u međuvremenu, server prekine vezu i zove korisnika nazad. "
"Informacije o ovjeri se šalju, i &kppp; čeka na komandnu liniju, a onda "
"počinje malu skriptu (ovdje se zove <filename>počnite_ppp</filename> koja "
"pokreće <application>pppd</application> na serveru."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <filename>start_ppp</filename> script might look something like the "
"following:"
msgstr "<filename>počnite_ppp</filename> skripta može izgledati kao sljedeće:"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: callback.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"stty -echo\n"
"exec /usr/sbin/pppd -detach silent modem"
msgstr ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"stty -echo\n"
"exec /usr/sbin/pppd -detach silent modem"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course, setting up a <acronym>PPP</acronym> server is not within the "
"scope of this document. For detailed information, see the <application>pppd</"
"application> man pages."
msgstr ""
"Naravno, postavljanje <application>PPP</application> servera nije u okviru "
"ovog dokumenta. Za detaljne informacije, pogledajte <application>pppd</"
"application> man stranice."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All other configuration issues, such as <application>pppd</application> "
"configuration or <acronym>IP</acronym> settings work as normal, and no "
"special software is required to pick up the line."
msgstr ""
"Sva ostala pitanja konfigurisanja, kao što su <application>pppd</"
"application> konfiguracija ili <application>IP</application> postavke rade "
"normalno, i nije potreban poseban softver za uzimanje linije."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kppp; callback and other programs such as <application>mgetty</application> "
"or any other faxgetty can be run on the same serial port. There are no "
"problems with the dial in, as &kppp; creates a lock file which will tell the "
"getty program that another application (in this case, &kppp; of course,) is "
"using the line at that time."
msgstr ""
"&kppp; povratnih poziva i drugih programa kao što su <application>mgetty</"
"application> ili bilo koji drugi faxgetty se može pokrenuti na istom "
"serijskom portu. Nema problema s biranjem, kada &kppp; stvara zatvorenu "
"datoteku koja će reći getty programu da druga aplikacija (u ovom slučaju, "
"&kppp; naravno,) koristi liniju u to vrijeme."

#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr "Rješavanje problema"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are some known problems with &kppp; in callback mode:"
msgstr "Postoje poznati problemi s &kppp; modom povratnih poziva:"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you initialize the modem to auto answer, you need to reset the modem "
"after your connection is closed. Otherwise, your modem will continue to pick "
"up the line for you, which is not a good idea if the line in question is "
"your main phone line."
msgstr ""
"Kada postavite modem da automatski odgovora, morate resetirati modem nakon "
"što se veza zatvori. U suprotnom, vaš modem će nastaviti da uzima liniju za "
"vas, što nije dobra ideja ako se radi o vašoj glavnoj telefonskoj liniji."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kppp; has some small problems when sharing a line with another program, "
"such as <application>mgetty</application>. If <application>mgetty</"
"application> is running on the same modem line, &kppp; is not able to "
"initialize the modem correctly."
msgstr ""
"&kppp; ima neke male probleme kada dijeli liniju sa nekim drugim programom, "
"kao što je <application>mgetty</application>. Ako <application>mgetty</"
"application> radi na istoj liniji modema, &kppp; nije u stanju da pravilno "
"inicijalizuje modem."

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kppp; is unable to prompt for certain user input during a scripting based "
"login. Unfortunately, when using the example script above, &kppp; also asks "
"for the user name the second time the callback server requests it. You can "
"get rid of this by hardcoding your userid into the login script (not very "
"portable or nice, but it works."
msgstr ""
"&kppp; nije u stanju da traži ulaz od korisnika tokom prijave bazirane na "
"skriptiranju. Nažalost, kada se koristi primjer skripte gore, &kppp; također "
"traži korisničko ime po drugi put kada to zatraži server povratnog poziva. "
"Možete se osloboditi ovog neposrednim upisivanjem vašeg korisničkog imena u "
"skriptu prijave (ne baš prijenosno ili lijepo, ali radi."

#. Tag: title
#: callback.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Windows; NT <acronym>RAS</acronym> callback"
msgstr "&Windows; NT <acronym>RAS</acronym> povratni poziv"

#. Tag: para
#: callback.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&Windows; NT uses a completely different approach than the one described "
"above. NT requires an extension to the <acronym>PPP</acronym> protocol "
"itself, called <acronym>CBCP</acronym> (Call Back Control Protocol). "
"<application>pppd</application> has support for this protocol, but you must "
"recompile <application>pppd</application>. If anybody has experience with "
"successfully connecting to an NT callback server, please let us know."
msgstr ""
"&Windows; NT koristi potpuno drugačiji pristup od onog gore opisanog. NT "
"zahtijeva produženje na <acronym>PPP</acronym> sopstveni protokol, pod "
"nazivom <acronym>CBCP</acronym> (Povratnog Poziva Kontrolni Protokol). "
"<application>pppd</application> ima podršku za ovaj protokol, ali morate da "
"rekompajlirate <application>pppd</application>. Ako neko ima iskustva sa "
"uspješnim povezivanjem na NT server za povratne pozive, javite nam."
